---
title: One Pot Lemon Pepper Chicken with Orzo
description: Lemon Pepper Chicken with Orzo is a zesty one-pot meal featuring juicy chicken thighs, orzo, feta, and lemon pepper for tons of flavor!
image: https://www.budgetbytes.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/One-Pot-Lemon-Pepper-Chicken-and-Orzo-H.jpg
cuisine: American
time required: 45 minutes
servings: 4
source: https://www.budgetbytes.com/lemon-pepper-chicken-with-orzo
course: Dinner, Main Course
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 35 minutes
tags: Chicken and orzo, lemon pepper chicken, One Pot Meal
nutrition:
  calories: 612 kcal
  fat: 32 g
  carbohydrates: 46 g
  protein: 34 g
  fiber: 3 g
  sodium: 715 mg
  serving size: 1 Serving
---

Blot the @chicken thighs{4}(dry with a paper towel), then season both sides liberally with @lemon pepper seasoning{2%tbsp}.

Heat a #large deep skillet{} over medium. Once hot, add @cooking oil{1%tbsp}. Add the seasoned @chicken thighs{}, skin side down, and let them cook undisturbed until browned (about ~{6-8%minutes} for bone-in skin-on thighs). Flip the @chicken thighs{} and cook until browned on the second side. The @chicken thighs{} will be cooked most of the way through at this point but will finish cooking when simmered with the @orzo{1.5%cups}. Remove the @chicken thighs{} to a clean plate.

While the @chicken thighs{} are browning, roughly chop about 1/4 bunch of @parsley{1/4%cup}(chopped) and mince @garlic{2%cloves}(minced). After removing the @chicken thighs{} from the skillet, turn the heat down to low, add the minced @garlic{}, and sauté the @garlic{} in the residual fat for about ~{1%minute}.

Add @chicken broth{2%cups} to the skillet and stir to dissolve the crispy browned bits from the bottom of the pan.

Add the @orzo{} and half of the chopped @parsley{}. Stir to combine. Finally, return the @chicken thighs{} to the skillet, skin side up.

Place a lid on the skillet, turn the heat up to high, and let the @chicken broth{} come to a full boil. Once it reaches a boil, turn the heat down to low. Let the skillet simmer on low for about ~{15%minutes}, or until most of the @chicken broth{} has been absorbed. Make sure it’s simmering the whole time. If it stops simmering, increase the heat slightly until it just starts to simmer again.

After about ~{15%minutes} the @orzo{} should be tender and most of the @chicken broth{} absorbed but there will still be a little sauce in the skillet.

Fluff the @orzo{} around the @chicken thighs{} a bit with a fork, then top with the remaining @parsley{} and @feta{2%oz}(crumbled). Serve and enjoy!
